ShaderEmu target (mkpkg.d shaderemu-setup shaderemu-build)
====================================

Machine: 32-bit RISC-V Linux, no MMU, static musl, rv32imaf (F, no D, no C),
ilp32 ABI (floats still passed in integer registers). The kernel only runs
bFLT flat executables. https://github.com/MichaelMoroz/ShaderEmu

Quick start (zig toolchain):
  1. download ShaderEmu into ./ShaderEmu (not part of this repo)
  2. ./mkpkg.d shaderemu-setup   one time: LDC runtime sources, zig, druntime
  3. ./mkpkg.d shaderemu-build   builds the .gz.b64.txt
Steps run left to right, so "./mkpkg.d shaderemu-setup shaderemu-build" does
both; --dry-run (-n) prints what each would do without changing anything.
Setup needs on PATH: a stock LDC with ldc-build-runtime (--ldc), curl, tar,
cmake, ninja; the build also python3 (for elf2bflt.py). Everything lands in
--work (default ~/ddhx-rv32), and both steps check what they need and say
what is missing. The numbered steps below are what shaderemu-setup does, for
doing it by hand or with the --toolchain shaderemu.


Status
------
Tested (Debian container, LDC 1.43.0 stock, zig 0.14.1): the zig toolchain
builds the runtime and ddhx, links, and elf2bflt produces a bFLT. The same
objects linked as a normal static-pie run under qemu-riscv32-static: --version
and the TUI render a file correctly. Not tested: the bFLT start path
(flatcrt.c) on ShaderEmu itself, and the --toolchain shaderemu (ShaderEmu gcc,
sysroot, libunwind), which needs a kernel build here.

Stock LDC has no riscv32 ABI ("unknown target ABI" warning) and passes every
struct byval/sret to C. ddhx and the Phobos paths it uses pass only scalars
and pointers to C, so this is expected to be fine; if the binary misbehaves at
a C call, suspect it first (LDC 1.43 gen/abi/riscv32.cpp would be needed).

Requirements
------------
- stock LDC (same version as the source tree below; 1.43.0 tested)
  and its ldc-build-runtime; cmake, ninja
- LDC source tarball extracted as WORK/ldc-1.43.0-src/ (only its runtime is
  built; the compiler itself is not rebuilt)
- ShaderEmu checkout (linux/nommu/elf2bflt.py); python3 to run it
- one of two C toolchains (default zig):
  shaderemu (untested): run ShaderEmu's linux/kernel/build.sh and
    linux/nommu/setup.sh once. Provides riscv32-linux-gcc
    (~/shaderemu-linux/toolchain/bin) and the musl 1.2.5 sysroot with
    compiler_rt (~/nm/work/sysroot), built with -march=rv32imaf -mabi=ilp32.
  zig (0.14.1 tested; pip "ziglang" or the tarball): musl, libunwind and the
    linker come from zig.

Setup
-----
1. Patch the runtime sources in WORK/ldc-1.43.0-src/runtime/ for rv32 + musl:
     druntime/src/core/sys/posix/signal.d
         MINSIGSTKSZ: "else version (RISCV64)" -> RISCV_Any
     druntime/src/core/stdc/fenv.d
         musl section, fenv_t/fexcept_t: RISCV64 -> RISCV_Any
     druntime/src/core/stdc/config.d
         muslRedirTime64 = false on RISCV32 (musl rv32 never had 32-bit
         time_t); add "else version (RISCV32)" after the Pre_Time64 case
     druntime/src/core/stdc/stdio.d
         drop pragma(printf)/pragma(scanf) on the v*printf/v*scanf
         declarations: without an riscv32 ABI the compiler has no va_list
         type to check them against:
           perl -0pi -e 's/pragma\((?:printf|scanf)\)\n(\s+int v\w*(?:printf|scanf)\()/$1/g' stdio.d
     phobos/std/math/hardware.d (line ~61)
         IeeeFlagsSupport: "else version (RISCV_Any)" -> RISCV64. LDC's
         FloatingPointControl.clearExceptions has no riscv case and hits a
         static assert otherwise.
   druntime/src/core/internal/backtrace/libunwind.d
         add a RISCV32 case: _LIBUNWIND_CONTEXT_SIZE = 64, _CURSOR_SIZE = 76
         (the RISCV64 values; opaque storage, oversize is harmless)
   Not needed with +f: core/thread/osthread.d (its fsw stores are valid on
   rv32 F).
2. Cross-build druntime + phobos into WORK/rt (rt/lib must hold the libs).
   The C compiler goes in as environment variables, not cmake variables, and
   -wi is needed because the missing-ABI warning is an error under the
   runtime's -w:
     CC=<cc> AR=<ar> ldc-build-runtime --ninja --buildDir=WORK/rt \
       --ldcSrcDir=WORK/ldc-1.43.0-src --targetSystem='Linux;musl;UNIX' \
       --dFlags='-mtriple=riscv32-unknown-linux-musl;-mattr=+m,+a,+f,-c,-d;-mabi=ilp32;-wi' \
       --cFlags=... BUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF CMAKE_AR=<ar> CMAKE_RANLIB=<ranlib>
   C toolchain, either:
     shaderemu: CC=riscv32-linux-gcc, --cFlags='-O2 -march=rv32imaf
                -mabi=ilp32 -fno-stack-protector -nostdinc
                -isystem <sysroot>/include -isystem <gcc include>'
     zig:       WORK/bin/rv32cc, rv32ar, rv32ranlib wrappers (no +f: zig's
                musl rv32 setjmp.S uses fsd, so it only builds soft-float;
                the D objects are +f and still link, both are ilp32):
                  exec zig cc -target riscv32-linux-musl -mcpu=generic_rv32+m+a "$@"
                  exec zig ar "$@"   /   exec zig ranlib "$@"
3. libunwind (druntime links -lunwind; the zig toolchain brings its own, the
   ShaderEmu sysroot has none). Untested for shaderemu: build LLVM 18.1.8
   libunwind (llvm-project releases: libunwind-18.1.8.src.tar.xz) as a static
   library with riscv32-linux-gcc/g++ and the same arch flags
   (-fno-exceptions -fno-rtti -nostdinc++; it relies on musl's
   dl_iterate_phdr, so do not define _LIBUNWIND_IS_BAREMETAL) and drop
   libunwind.a into WORK/rt/lib. If this fights back, use --toolchain zig.

Expected layout
---------------
  WORK/ldc-VERSION-src/ (VERSION = --ldc's)  WORK/rt/lib/  [./ShaderEmu/]
  shaderemu: --gcc (riscv32-linux-gcc), --sysroot
  zig:       WORK/bin/rv32cc

Build
-----
  ./mkpkg.d shaderemu-setup [--work DIR] [--ldc PATH]
  ./mkpkg.d shaderemu-build [--work DIR] [--ldc PATH] [--shaderemu DIR]
                      [--toolchain zig] [--gcc PATH] [--sysroot DIR]

Using the output
----------------
Upload the .gz.b64.txt, open it in ShaderEmu's browser, "Save page as"
/root/ddhx.b64, then:
  base64 -d /root/ddhx.b64 | gunzip > /root/ddhx && chmod +x /root/ddhx

flatcrt.c is the bFLT start file (after ShaderEmu's linux/nommu/flatcrt.c)
plus AT_PHDR/AT_PHNUM/AT_PHENT so musl's TLS setup and D's dl_iterate_phdr
find the program headers. Its entry is _flat_start, so it does not collide
with the _start of the C library's startup file.
